# bitcoinix release signing keys, in ssh-keygen(1) ALLOWED SIGNERS format.
#
# This file is the authoritative list. The fingerprints of its keys are documented in
# ../../SECURITY.md and test/release-keys-test.sh fails if the two drift.
#
# helper/fetch-release.sh verifies release tags against this file. To verify by hand:
#   git config gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile helper/release-keys/ssh-allowed-signers
#   git config gpg.ssh.revocationFile helper/release-keys/ssh-revoked-keys
#   git tag -v v<version>
#
# To retire a key, do NOT delete its line: append valid-before="YYYYMMDD" so that
# tags signed while the key was still valid keep verifying. valid-before is checked
# against the tag's own date, so it does not stop a COMPROMISED key: add that key to
# ssh-revoked-keys (and keep its line here).
#
# Do not use empty lines, separate entries with a bare "#" instead: some OpenSSH
# versions report an empty line as "missing key" when parsing this file.
#
